stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB

    [*] --> Plugged

    Plugged --> SlacMatching : duty in (4,7)
    Plugged --> Plugged : ISO, duty in (7,97) arms iso_pwm_wait_s once
    Plugged --> Charging : PWM deadline, AC ISO falls back to AcIec
    Plugged --> Faulted : PWM deadline, DC Internal "no 5 % PWM"

    note right of SlacMatching
        MCS: CP C for 4 s, then B,
        then trigger_matching and arm 30s deadline.
    end note

    SlacMatching --> V2GNegotiating : SlacState=MATCHED
    SlacMatching --> Faulted : StateDeadline (30s, SlacTimeout)

    V2GNegotiating --> Charging : IsoPowerReady (AC)
    V2GNegotiating --> Charging : IsoDcPowerOn / dc_power_on (DC)
    V2GNegotiating --> V2GNegotiating : IsoPowerReady (DC, CP=C + power-on, await dc_power_on)
    V2GNegotiating --> Stopping : IsoStopFromCharger
    V2GNegotiating --> Faulted : StateDeadline (60s, V2GTimeout)

    Charging --> Paused : PauseSession / IsoPauseFromCharger
    Charging --> Stopping : StopSession / IsoStopFromCharger / IsoV2GFinished
    Charging --> Faulted : InternalFault

    Paused --> BcbToggling : ResumeSession (no live ISO session, seeds bcb_remaining=6)
    Paused --> Paused : ResumeSession (ISO session live, defer + arm 15s fallback)
    Paused --> BcbToggling : IsoV2GFinished (release deferred resume)
    Paused --> BcbToggling : StateDeadline (15s deferred-resume fallback)
    Paused --> Stopping : StateDeadline (1h watchdog)
    Paused --> Faulted : InternalFault

    BcbToggling --> V2GNegotiating : 6x StateDeadline (link kept, DC D-LINK_PAUSE)
    BcbToggling --> SlacMatching : 6x StateDeadline + slac_unmatched (re-match)
    BcbToggling --> Faulted : InternalFault

    Stopping --> [*] : IsoV2GFinished / StateDeadline (10s), held without a session
    Stopping --> Plugged : charger stop, SLAC reset, same session awaits a fresh 5 % PWM edge
    Stopping --> Faulted : InternalFault

    note right of Paused
        CP held at C while an ISO session is still
        tearing down, lowered to B when the EVCC
        receives PowerDeliveryRes (V2gMessage). IsoV2GFinished
        re-asserts B as a backstop for peers that
        publish no per-message signal.
    end note
